name 'iterating-with-ai-preassessment-q2_2025'

question 'When writing pseudocode for a loop, what is a "stopping condition"?'

wrong 'The first line of code that starts the loop.'
right 'The rule that determines when the loop should end so it doesn\'t run forever.'
wrong 'A comment that explains what the loop does to other developers.'
wrong 'The part of the code that displays the final result on the screen.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 1

Without a clear stopping condition, a loop could become an "infinite loop," causing the program to crash or freeze.
MARKDOWN
